rust-widgets-font — font data notice
====================================

This crate ships **font data**, not code, and none of that data is under the MIT licence that
covers the crate's own source. Every payload is a subset of a font released under the
SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org/), and each subset is a
"Modified Version" under that licence: it retains a portion of the upstream glyphs, it is
renamed, and it does not use the upstream Reserved Font Name.

This file is the authoritative prose record for every font payload behind this crate's
features: what was subset, what was dropped, and the licence reasoning per face. The shard index
that lives in the library (`src/render/text/font_assets/cjk_shards.rs`) is recorded here too,
because its only content is the names of these shards. The repository-root `NOTICE`
(https://github.com/mikewolfli/rust-widgets/blob/main/NOTICE) records the material that is not a
font payload — the GNU Unifont bitmap table and the Material Symbols icon outlines — and
`tools/check_font_licenses.sh` reads both files, so a generated table's header and the record that
names it cannot drift apart.

Payloads
--------

    src/latin.rs / latin.ttf            Open Sans (Google Fonts)
    src/arabic.rs / arabic.ttf          Noto Naskh Arabic
    src/cjk.rs / cjk.ttf                Noto Sans SC
    src/cjk_shard_*.rs / *.ttf          Noto Sans SC, partitioned by Unicode block
    src/emoji.rs / emoji.ttf            Noto Color Emoji

Each face is recorded in full below.

