Noto Sans SC (sharded) — unicode-range subsets for `fonts-cjk-shards`
================================================================================

Included files
    src/render/text/font_assets/cjk_shards.rs             (the shard index, generated; stays in the library)
    crates/rust-widgets-font/src/cjk_shard_latin.rs/ttf    (the Latin shard)
    crates/rust-widgets-font/src/cjk_shard_symbols.rs/ttf  (the CJK Symbols and Punctuation shard)
    crates/rust-widgets-font/src/cjk_shard_kana.rs/ttf     (the kana shard)
    crates/rust-widgets-font/src/cjk_shard_han.rs/ttf      (the Han shard)
    crates/rust-widgets-font/src/cjk_shard_fullwidth.rs/ttf (the fullwidth-forms shard)

Origin
    Noto Sans SC, by the Noto project (Adobe and Google). The **same** upstream
    revision as the `fonts-cjk` face above:
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/main/Sans/SubsetOTF/SC/NotoSansSC-Regular.otf
        SHA-256 of the upstream `.otf`:
            faa6c9df652116dde789d351359f3d7e5d2285a2b2a1f04a2d7244df706d5ea9

    The files are generated, never hand-edited. Regenerate with:
        python3 tools/gen_cjk_shards.py --license=ofl-1.1

What it is
    The `fonts-cjk` face's codepoints, **partitioned** on Unicode block boundaries
    rather than shipped as one file. The union of the shards is exactly
    `tools/cjk_vector_codepoints.txt` — the same coverage as `cjk.ttf` — and
    `tools/check_cjk_shards_cover_the_face.sh` asserts that equality codepoint for
    codepoint, so the sharded build and the one-face build render the same
    characters. The boundaries are declared in `tools/cjk_vector_shards.txt`.

    Sharding is a *packaging* of the same payload, not a different subset: a host
    that draws one script (say Japanese) can enable `fonts-cjk-shard-kana` and load
    only that shard, instead of carrying every CJK glyph the face contains. Each
    shard is a separate `include_bytes!` behind its own `fonts-cjk-shard-<id>`
    feature; the total when every shard is enabled (411,180 bytes) is slightly
    larger than the one-face build (361,704 bytes) because each subset carries its
    own copy of the shared layout tables. No outline or layout table was modified.

Licence
    SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
        https://openfontlicense.org/

Reserved Font Name (OFL)
    As for `fonts-cjk` above, Noto Sans SC declares no Reserved Font Name; the shard
    files are named after this crate's modules and the shard id, not after the
    upstream family. The name "Noto Sans SC" appears in this NOTICE and in the
    generated file headers for attribution only.

Embedding exception
-------------------

The OFL's "embedding exception" is what permits these files to be converted into, and shipped as,
binary payloads inside a software distribution. Nothing here is sold on its own, and the fonts are
not the product.

Why the data lives here
-----------------------

The library that consumes it (`rust_widgets`) is capped at 10 MiB per package by crates.io, and
these payloads are already-compressed binaries that gzip cannot shrink. Keeping them in a package
of their own is what lets the library keep growing. Nothing about the licence changes with the
move: the same bytes, the same subsets, the same upstream revisions.
